---
import { Highlighter, List, MessageSquare, Printer, Square, Undo2 } from '@inkbar/icons'

import Icon from '../site/Icon.astro'
---

<section id="features">
  <div class="container inner">
    <div class="intro">
      <h2>What it does today.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Inkbar covers viewing, search, outlines and links, sidebars, forms, signatures,
        highlights, note threads, drawing, redaction marks, plugins, printing and
        downloads. It works by touch, opens password-protected files and ships in English,
        French and German. Everything below works in every framework package and with no
        framework.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 3h9l4 4v14H6zM15 3v4h4"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Viewing</h3>
        <p>
          Pages render on PDF.js with a selectable text layer. Fit to width or page, zoom
          from 10% to 800%, and scroll continuously or a page at a time. Only pages near
          the viewport are mounted.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
          <path d="M21 21l-4.3-4.3"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Search</h3>
        <p>
          Press Ctrl/Cmd+F in the viewer and type. Every match highlights and the count
          updates as pages scan. <code>doc.search</code> hands your code the same matches,
          with where each one sits on the page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={List} />
        <h3>Outline and links</h3>
        <p>
          The document's bookmarks show as a tree you can move through by keyboard. Links
          on the page work with no setup and Tab reaches each one. Back and Forward return
          you to where you were before a jump.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"></rect>
          <path d="M9 4v16"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Sidebars</h3>
        <p>
          Put panels of thumbnails, search results or your own content beside the pages.
          Drag the edge or use the arrow keys to resize. When the window gets narrow, a
          rail panel floats over the pages.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"></rect>
          <path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Forms</h3>
        <p>
          Fill text fields, checkboxes, radio buttons, lists and signature fields. The
          form's own scripts calculate totals and check input, and your code reads and
          sets the values through <code>doc.form</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3 17c3-6 5-9 6-7s-2 7 0 7 3-5 5-5 1 4 3 4 2-2 4-2M3 21h18"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Signatures</h3>
        <p>
          Draw a signature, type it in a handwriting font or upload a scan. Inkbar keeps
          it in the store you choose and places it on any page or in a signature field.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={Highlighter} />
        <h3>Highlights</h3>
        <p>
          With the Highlight tool on, select text and it is highlighted when you let go.
          From the keyboard, select text and press Enter.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={MessageSquare} />
        <h3>Note threads</h3>
        <p>Pin a note to the page, then reply, edit and delete in a thread beside it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={Square} />
        <h3>Redaction marks</h3>
        <p>
          Mark selected text, or drag a box over any area. A mark records what to remove.
          Inkbar will remove the content once saving into the PDF ships.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 20h9M16.5 3.5a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4z"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Drawing</h3>
        <p>
          Draw freehand, add lines, arrows, rectangles, ellipses, stars and polygons, and
          type into text boxes. A freehand stroke that looks like a shape snaps into one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8 4H6v16h2M16 4h2v16h-2M10 9h4M10 13h4"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Annotations as data</h3>
        <p>
          Export and import JSON with a published schema. Underline, strikeout, squiggly,
          ink, shapes, lines and text boxes from imported data display too, and the PDF's
          own annotations show as locked.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M15.39 4.39a1 1 0 0 0 1.68-.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 1 3.014 3.015 1 1 0 0 0-.474 1.68l1.683 1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 0 3.414L19.61 15.39a1 1 0 0 1-1.68-.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 0-3.014 3.015 1 1 0 0 1 .474 1.68l-1.683 1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1-3.414 0L8.61 19.61a1 1 0 0 0-1.68.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 1-3.014-3.015 1 1 0 0 0 .474-1.68l-1.683-1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 0-3.414L4.39 8.61a1 1 0 0 1 1.68.474 2.5 2.5 0 1 0 3.014-3.015 1 1 0 0 1-.474-1.68l1.683-1.682a2.414 2.414 0 0 1 3.414 0z"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Plugins</h3>
        <p>
          A plugin adds commands, tools and page layers, listens for presses and keeps
          records of its own. Each record can show as a mark that opens a card, and the
          same cards list in a sidebar. One plugin runs in every framework package.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={Undo2} />
        <h3>Undo and redo</h3>
        <p>
          History with grouped steps, whether Inkbar holds the annotations or your app
          does, and field edits undo too. Press Ctrl/Cmd+Z, or put the undo and redo
          buttons wherever your toolbar has room.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="5" r="1.6"></circle>
          <path d="M5 9h14M12 9v5M8 21l4-7 4 7"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Keyboard and screen readers</h3>
        <p>
          Fill fields, highlight, add notes, and move, resize or delete marks from the
          keyboard, with labelled controls throughout. Area marks and freehand drawing
          need a pointer.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 11V5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 0v5M12 10V8.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 0V11M15 11a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 0v3a7 7 0 0 1-7 7h-.5a6 6 0 0 1-4.6-2.2L3.6 16a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 2.3-1.9L9 17"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Touch</h3>
        <p>
          Pinch to zoom the document, not the browser page, on a touch screen or trackpad.
          With a drawing tool on, one finger draws and two fingers scroll.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="2"></rect>
          <path d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Locked files</h3>
        <p>
          When a PDF needs a password, a dialog asks for it, with nothing to set up. The
          password is used once and never stored. Turn the prompt off to run your own
          flow.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <Icon icon={Printer} />
        <h3>Print and download</h3>
        <p>
          Press Ctrl/Cmd+P to print or Ctrl/Cmd+S to download, or use the toolbar buttons.
          Both give you the PDF as it was opened. Annotations go in once saving into the
          PDF ships.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
          <path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.6 3.8 5.6 3.8 9s-1.3 6.4-3.8 9c-2.5-2.6-3.8-5.6-3.8-9S9.5 5.6 12 3z"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Translations</h3>
        <p>
          French and German ship with Inkbar, and any other language is a set of strings
          you pass in. Change one string or all of them. A new language relabels the
          viewer in place, with no remount and no lost scroll position.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="next">
      <h3>On the way</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Saving annotations, field values and applied redactions into the PDF</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .inner {
    container-type: inline-size;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 48px;
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 112px);
  }
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.2vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  /*
   * One, two or three equal columns. Each cell draws the line on its right and below it,
   * except on the outer edge, where the grid's own border is. A short last row leaves blank
   * paper rather than stretching its cells. The first cell of the last row is the one in the
   * first column that is also among the last n cells.
   */
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--sheet);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--sheet);
  }
  .cell:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  @container (min-width: 540px) and (max-width: 859.98px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
    .cell {
      border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .cell:nth-child(2n) {
      border-right: 0;
    }
    .cell:nth-child(2n + 1):nth-last-child(-n + 2),
    .cell:nth-child(2n + 1):nth-last-child(-n + 2) ~ .cell {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  @container (min-width: 860px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
    .cell {
      border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .cell:nth-child(3n) {
      border-right: 0;
    }
    .cell:nth-child(3n + 1):nth-last-child(-n + 3),
    .cell:nth-child(3n + 1):nth-last-child(-n + 3) ~ .cell {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px 32px;
  }
  .next ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .next li {
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--caption);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--body);
  }
</style>
